README (doc-writer), after k104/k59 land:
1. File-tool path rules (Read/Write/Edit/MultiEdit/NotebookEdit) must be absolute (${PROJECT_DIR} or a full path) and below a root; relative or root-only rules are a load error; the bare tool name means every path. On Windows use a drive letter: a drive-less Write(/etc/*) never matches C:\ paths.
2. Allowlist mode: a command with an output redirection is only allowed by a rule that spells it out (Bash(echo x > *)); fd duplication (2>&1) and the null device do not count; Bash(*) no longer covers redirections, bare Bash does.
3. k59 item 2: tool-native escapes no command-line matcher sees — git -c core.pager/core.sshCommand/alias.x=!sh, GIT_*/PAGER/EDITOR env, find -exec/-execdir/-delete, xargs from a file, tar --to-command/--checkpoint-action, rsync -e, ssh -o ProxyCommand, awk system(), sed -i / sed e, tee/cp/dd of=/Out-File/Set-Content, python -c/node -e/perl -e, npm/make scripts. Bash(git *) grants all of these.
4. On Windows path rules ignore case, and .. cannot climb above a \\server\share root.
Also the unreagent-config skill if it describes the permission rule format.

